-- An assumption may refer to the previous values of the outputs. When it
-- does not hold, the function is relieved of the guarantees from then on:
-- here, after an output of 0, the next input is assumed to be nonzero. The
-- function y = (if x = 0 then 0 else 1) realizes the contract, although no
-- function satisfies the guarantees on the input trace <0, 0>, on which the
-- assumption fails at the second step.

function imported F(x: int) returns (y: int);
(*@contract
  assume true -> (pre y = 0 => x <> 0);
  guarantee x = 0 => y = 0;
  guarantee true -> (pre x = 0 => y = 1);
*)
